  ⚠ unicorn(no-negated-comparison): Unexpected negated comparison.
   ╭─[no_negated_comparison.ts:1:22]
 1 │ const foo = <boolean>!(a === b);
   ·                      ──────────
   ╰────
  help: Use the opposite comparison operator instead of negating the whole comparison.

  ⚠ unicorn(no-negated-comparison): Unexpected negated comparison.
   ╭─[no_negated_comparison.ts:2:1]
 1 │ foo
 2 │ !(<boolean>a === b)
   · ───────────────────
   ╰────
  help: Use the opposite comparison operator instead of negating the whole comparison.

  ⚠ unicorn(no-negated-comparison): Unexpected negated logical expression of comparisons.
   ╭─[no_negated_comparison.ts:1:22]
 1 │ const foo = <boolean>!(a === b && c === d);
   ·                      ─────────────────────
   ╰────
  help: Apply De Morgan's law: negate each comparison and swap `&&`/`||` instead of negating the whole expression.
